            <ArticleTitle>Pelvic gliomatosis within foci of endometriosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>267-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The third reported case of pelvic gliomatosis found within foci of endometriosis is documented 16 years after the removal of a benign cystic teratoma. Grossly at laparoscopy the lesions appear as typical deep fibrotic endometriotic implants.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
